---
import ContentPageLayout from '../layouts/ContentPageLayout.astro';
---
<ContentPageLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="MiniAdda's editorial standards: accuracy, sourcing, corrections and verification."
  heading="Editorial Policy"
  crumb="Editorial Policy"
>
  <p>
    These standards apply to every article published on MiniAdda.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We publish facts we can verify. When something is uncertain, developing or disputed, we say so
    plainly rather than implying more certainty than exists.
  </p>

  <h2>Sourcing</h2>
  <p>
    Where an answer relies on reporting or data, we link to the source. Sources are named,
    reachable and relevant — not decorative links.
  </p>

  <h2>Verification dates</h2>
  <p>
    Each article shows a <em>last verified</em> date. We re-check time-sensitive answers (elections,
    prices, product releases) and update them when the facts change.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If we get something wrong, we correct it and, where meaningful, note the change. To report an
    error, <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>
    Editorial content is not for sale. We do not publish paid placements disguised as answers, and
    we do not fabricate reviews, authors or citations.
  </p>

  <h2>AI and automation</h2>
  <p>
    Drafting tools may assist, but a human editor reviews and approves every published answer, and
    remains responsible for its accuracy.
  </p>
</ContentPageLayout>
